<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the app says about itself to macOS, over and above what the bundler writes.

  **macOS puts items into the Edit menu that this app never wrote** — Writing Tools, AutoFill, Start
  Dictation…, Emoji & Symbols — and it writes them in whatever language the reader's machine and this
  bundle have in common. A bundle naming no localizations has only its development region to offer,
  so that language was English, and those items stood in English beside the ones Amenbo had already
  drawn in the reader's own (`AMB-T-4464` measured it on four builds).

  **Naming the nineteen is the whole of the fix** (`AMB-D-394`). Empty `.lproj` directories are not
  needed for it: measured, the same items come out translated on the declaration alone, and a build
  carrying both lists every language twice for nothing.

  **This file is picked up because it sits beside `tauri.conf.json`.** `tauri-cli` merges what is
  here into the Info.plist the bundler generates, and `tauri.conf.json` names it nowhere on purpose:
  the Makefile injects `bundle.macOS.files` through `--config` on every build, and a second writer of
  that object would put the merge order in play for no gain.

  ⚠ **Which of the nineteen is still the machine's answer, not Amenbo's.** These items follow the
  OS's `AppleLanguages`, and the language a reader picked in Amenbo does not enter into it — so a
  macOS in English with an Amenbo in Japanese draws one menu in two languages. Closing that would
  mean writing `AppleLanguages` into the app's own defaults, which is a decision and not a file.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Where a reader whose language is not on the list below lands, which is where the dictionary drops
    them too (`AMB-D-394`). Spelt `en` rather than the `English` the bundler defaults to: the two name
    the same region, but one of them reads as the fallback it is.
  -->
  <key>CFBundleDevelopmentRegion</key>
  <string>en</string>
  <!--
    The nineteen, in the order `AMB-D-394` sets them out: the two Amenbo began with, then the nine it
    reaches most readers with, then the eight after those.
  -->
  <key>CFBundleLocalizations</key>
  <array>
    <string>en</string>
    <string>ja</string>
    <string>zh-Hans</string>
    <string>zh-Hant</string>
    <string>ko</string>
    <string>es</string>
    <string>pt-BR</string>
    <string>fr</string>
    <string>de</string>
    <string>it</string>
    <string>ru</string>
    <string>hi</string>
    <string>id</string>
    <string>vi</string>
    <string>th</string>
    <string>tr</string>
    <string>pl</string>
    <string>nl</string>
    <string>uk</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
